\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{A bound on the retained space}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{In \ref{fdip-00K4}, the eliminated plane contains a whole
line of zero energy, while the retained space is the specified
line #{X=\mathbb Qe_1}. The [Loewner comparison](fdip-00K1)
allows us to ask for a nonnegative self-adjoint operator bounded
by #{A} whose values all lie in #{X}. How can we characterize a
greatest operator with these properties?}
